From: Osvaldo Janeri Filho <janeri@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:41:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 62/89] Prevent unsigned integer overflow in IAKERB

In iakerb_save_token(), check that token->length (size_t) won't
overflow the accumulated conversation length ctx->conv.length
(unsigned int).

[ghudson@mit.edu: edited commit message]

ticket: 9278 (new)
tags: pullup
target_version: 1.22-next

(cherry picked from commit 32c1d65f56af1b6c150497a4f9d322a50c2a9f05)
---
 src/lib/gssapi/krb5/iakerb.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lib/gssapi/krb5/iakerb.c b/src/lib/gssapi/krb5/iakerb.c
index a0d298c49e..b3e9212be2 100644
--- a/src/lib/gssapi/krb5/iakerb.c
+++ b/src/lib/gssapi/krb5/iakerb.c
@@ -147,6 +147,9 @@ iakerb_save_token(iakerb_ctx_id_t ctx, const gss_buffer_t token)
 {
     char *p;
 
+    if (token->length > UINT_MAX - ctx->conv.length)
+        return ENOMEM;
+
     p = realloc(ctx->conv.data, ctx->conv.length + token->length);
     if (p == NULL)
         return ENOMEM;
-- 
